{
  // Courier / workshop / red parcel, told with NO REFERENCES AT ALL (epic 24017, sc-24025).
  //
  // The same six-beat story as `plan.jsonc`, against `references.described.jsonc` — a pack whose
  // roles are words and nothing else. Every shot is `text_to_video`: no shot binds a
  // `referenceRole`, and unlike `plan.jsonc` no shot takes a keyframe either, so nothing in this
  // production is conditioned on an image and every shot resolves to the base `minimax_h3`
  // checkpoint.
  //
  // That is the point of the document. With no picture anywhere, the ONLY thing holding the
  // courier, the recipient, the parcel and the room together across six cuts is that the compiler
  // writes the pack's description of each of them into every prompt that lists them in
  // `continuityRoles`, word for word, identically. The prompts below deliberately do NOT re-describe
  // them: they say what happens, and let the identity text say who it happens to. A prompt that
  // spelled out "a young woman in a blue quilted jacket" itself would be the drift this fixture
  // exists to demonstrate the absence of.
  //
  // `recipient` appears in the last three shots and in none of the first three, so the difference
  // between a shot that locks a role and one that does not is visible within one film.
  //
  // No sound pack, so no beds and no placed dialogue: the shots state their own sound in `audio`,
  // which is what MiniMax-H3 scores from. Schema 3 (sc-24026): `audio` is required on every shot.
  //
  // THIS IS THE TURBO NO-REFERENCE EVALUATION FILM (sc-24029). Turbo is the path a user takes —
  // the 50-step base regime renders this film in hours — so the evaluation of the text identity
  // lock is done on the regime it will actually be read on, and the plan declares the accelerator
  // itself rather than leaving it to a flag nobody passes. `model.loras` names only the BASE
  // partition's adapter because that is the only partition this film has: no shot binds a
  // reference role, so every shot resolves to `minimax_h3`. `model.advanced.steps` is deliberately
  // unset, exactly as in `plan.v2.turbo.jsonc` — omitted, the recipe's own 4 governs, and setting
  // it would override the count the adapter was distilled for. `plan.jsonc` remains the 50-step
  // base regime a turbo take is judged against.
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "courier-workshop-described",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "Courier at the Workshop (described)",
  "synopsis": "A courier enters a cluttered workshop carrying a red parcel, sets it on the workbench and leaves; the recipient comes in, finds the parcel and opens it.",
  "model": {
    "id": "minimax_h3",
    "tier": "q4",
    "fps": 24,
    "resolution": "576x320",
    // Declared once on the FAMILY, as `plan.v2.turbo.jsonc` declares its pair; the compiler routes
    // each id to the partitions its catalog entry allows. Only the base-partition entry is named
    // here because no shot in this film binds a reference role, so `minimax_h3` is the only
    // partition anything dispatches as. 4 NFE, video shift 12, audio shift 3, 544p training canvas
    // — the same v0.1 schedule the reference film's turbo pair uses, so the two are comparable.
    "loras": ["minimax_h3_turbo_4step_v01"]
  },
  "limits": {
    "maxRunSeconds": 7200,
    "maxShotSeconds": 2700,
    "maxAttemptsPerShot": 1,
    "maxMemoryGb": 96
  },
  "shots": [
